Teams notifications from SharePoint
When a new item is added or modified in a SharePoint list (e.g. a new project, support ticket, or sales lead), post a formatted message to a specific Teams channel so the team sees it instantly.

Email attachment archival
Save attachments from specific senders (e.g. vendors, clients) into a designated SharePoint or OneDrive folder, with file names auto-tagged by sender and date. Save all attachments from specific senders to a OneDrive folder.


Scheduled reports / digests
Every Monday morning, query a SharePoint list or Excel file, build a summary, and email it to leadership — pending approvals, overdue tasks, weekly KPIs, etc. Removes manual report compilation.

Task creation from flagged emails
When you flag an email in Outlook, automatically create a task in Planner or To Do with the email subject, body, and link — keeps your inbox clean and your  list complete.